# Don't ship local build artifacts into the Docker context — Railway must build fresh.
# If these are copied in, turbo sees a cache hit and skips rebuilding workspace packages,
# which means stale `dist/` from the developer's machine ends up running in production.

# Dependencies — re-installed inside the image
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Compiled output — re-emitted inside the image
**/dist
**/.next
**/build
**/.output
**/.nitro

# Turbo cache — must NOT be carried in; it tells turbo "already built" for stale source
.turbo
**/.turbo

# TypeScript incremental
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Local env files (secrets come from Railway env / Secrets Manager)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example

# Version control / editor metadata
# NOTE: do NOT exclude .gitignore — docker/Dockerfile.backend's builder stage
# does `COPY .gitignore .gitignore`, and `turbo prune --docker` respects it
# when emitting out/full/. Excluding it breaks the build.
.git
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# Terraform — never needed in app images
infra/terraform/.terraform
infra/terraform/*.tfstate
infra/terraform/*.tfstate.*
infra/terraform/*.tfplan
infra/terraform/*.tfvars
infra/terraform/.secrets

# Test / debug artifacts
coverage
*.log
*.pem
*.stackdump
.playwright-mcp
